Z||000000||lamboman||11-29-2001||02:33 AM||||Hello Everyone:<BR>     I am converting my 1985 2.5 to a 2.8L<BR>for my lambo project. I have everything i need except transmission , Clutch / Pressure plate and flywheel. I am wondering if I can use the four speed transmission off my 1984 fiero with the 2.5L engine and also if I can use the clutch / pressure plate and flywheel.<P>I have heard i can use all the parts and they will bolt up to the 2.8 , I am not sure about the flywheel though.<P>Thanks:<BR>Trevor||||reg||1
Z||000001||jelly2m8||11-29-2001||11:06 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lamboman:<BR><B>Hello Everyone:<BR>     I am converting my 1985 2.5 to a 2.8L<BR>for my lambo project. I have everything i need except transmission , Clutch / Pressure plate and flywheel. I am wondering if I can use the four speed transmission off my 1984 fiero with the 2.5L engine and also if I can use the clutch / pressure plate and flywheel.<P>I have heard i can use all the parts and they will bolt up to the 2.8 , I am not sure about the flywheel though.<P>Thanks:<BR>Trevor</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> You will need a flywheel for the 2.8 motor.<BR>85-87 2.8 flywheels are interchangable,they are all balanced. But the 88 uses a neturally balanced flywheel.<P> The 2.5 4 spd clutch will work on the 2.8 flywheel. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
